 "notes": "Tables are matched by the stated TableName prefix (the stage suffix is rendered as <param:stage>, or the stage default when one is given); targets are tied to their table by ref, indexes by the stated index name inside ResourceId. The stage parameter is matched by a name containing 'stage'. That the suffix equals the stage value is checked only as a non-empty '-<suffix>' because a Ref to the parameter resolves to its default. Index-level scaling targets are detail: the prompt lists them as an extension of the table scaling, which is core. outputs_count accepts all-Ref or all-literal table-name outputs; a mix of the two forms would fail it (detail)."
